From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 08:04:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 026/155] [ae-patch] Put a pull request card's chips, outcome
 and action on one wrapping row

Reid's second note (2026-09-27) that the cards waste space: at 1200 px the
compact card under a chat message put every piece on its own full-width
row, the right two-thirds empty (the chips, GitHub's "Pull Request
successfully merged" echo, the "1 more open pull request" note, the
conflict reason, a tall disabled Merge).

AePrCards.tsx only (patch 0012's file), no upstream file touched:
- One status row (data-testid="ae-pr-status-row"): the chips, then the
  outcome or the reason Merge is off, then Merge or Mark session done at
  the right end (ml-auto). Each part is flex 1 1 auto, so it stays beside
  the chips when it fits and wraps to its own row only when it does not.
- Merged reads "Merged (squashed) b0413d6"; GitHub's message is dropped,
  and the "N more open pull requests" note is an inline muted span.
- Buttons are h-8 with a mouse and h-10 on a coarse pointer (the
  Dashboard's .btn), not h-11 below md; Merge no longer spans a phone card.
- The card's padding is px-2 py-1.5 and its row gap 1 (was p-2, 1.5).

Tests: the status row holds the chips, the reason and a compact Merge; the
merged line has no echo and sits on the row with the note.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
